# Line-ending policy.
#
# The production target is Linux (Pi 5, Debian 13, aarch64) and CI runs there too,
# while development happens on Windows. Without this file git stores LF but checks
# out CRLF on Windows, so the same commit produces different bytes per platform —
# which would make `cargo fmt --check`, fixture hashes and any byte-exact wire test
# platform-dependent. Everything textual is therefore normalized to LF in the
# repository *and* in the working tree, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary fixtures: never touch these. The two Anvil fixtures are byte-exact copies of
# vanilla output and are compared by hash (P03-05), so any translation would break
# them. The `.hex` fixtures are text but are golden wire bytes, so they are listed
# explicitly as text to keep them diffable while still LF.
*.mca binary
*.dat binary
*.png binary
*.jar binary

# Rust and docs are text; listed for clarity rather than necessity.
*.rs text
*.toml text
*.md text
*.tsv text
*.hex text
*.lock text
*.yml text
